# Review: BrainPlugin

The store seam is solid: `makeFactStoreRegistry` builds one lazily created in-memory `FactStore`
per space, a space-affinity `LayerSpec` serves the same instance to operations, and `QueryFacts` and
`SummarizeSubject` are implemented as visible operations with unit tests for filtering, the limit,
grounding and the empty-subject case. The `org.dxos.skill.brain` skill lists both tools.

The plugin has moved past the spec in two places. The facts panel is a role-only surface
(`BrainSurface.Facts`) that reads the active space, not a companion over an article subject, and
`FactViewer` comes from `@dxos/react-ui-rdf`, not `src/components`. The F-4 consumers no longer live
in plugin-inbox: fact extraction is brain's own `AnalyzeMailbox`, contributed as an inbox
`MailboxProcessor`, and `GenerateReply` is a brain operation contributed through
`InboxCapabilities.ReplyGenerator`. The dependency runs brain → inbox, so the "no inbox → brain"
property holds, but `EnrichMailbox` as the spec names it is gone. The skill instructions also carry a
"Procedure (do this first)" recipe, against F-2.2.

Of 25 items: 12 done, 4 untested, 4 partial, 4 diverged, 1 missing.

